{"title":"Smallest Number With Given Digit Product","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"Given a positive integer n, return a string representing the smallest positive integer such that the product of its digits is equal to n, or \"-1\" if no such number exists.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: n = 10^5\nOutput: \"357\"\n```\n\n3 * 5 * 7 = 10^5. It can be shown that 357 is the smallest number with a product of digits equal to 10^5. So the answer would be \"357\".\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: n = 7\nOutput: \"7\"\n```\n\nSince 7 has only one digit, its product of digits would be 7. We will show that 7 is the smallest number with a product of digits equal to 7. Since the product of numbers 1 to 6 is 1 to 6 respectively, so \"7\" would be the answer.\n\n### Example 3\n\n```text\nInput: n = 44\nOutput: \"-1\"\n```\n\nIt can be shown that there is no number such that its product of digits is equal to 44. So the answer would be \"-1\".\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= n <= 10^18\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn the smallest decimal string whose digit product is n, or \"-1\" if none exists.","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def smallestNumber(self, n: int) -> str:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().smallestNumber","parameters":[{"name":"n","type":"int"}],"returnType":"str","tests":[{"input":[{"$bigint":"1"}],"expected":"1"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"10"}],"expected":"25"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"1000000000000000000"}],"expected":"555555555555555555888888"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"10344086099751346"}],"expected":"-1"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"1050"}],"expected":"5567"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"105683697621228957"}],"expected":"-1"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"106347107784275963"}],"expected":"-1"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"1080"}],"expected":"3589"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"108546093483443553"}],"expected":"-1"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"111032366495713610"}],"expected":"-1"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"111322369595742470"}],"expected":"-1"},{"input":[{"$bigint":"112"}],"expected":"2